# Reviewable, expiring exceptions for the CI vulnerability gate. One CVE per
# line, each with: why it is a false positive or not applicable, and a
# re-check date.

# CVE-2025-59250 — com.microsoft.sqlserver:mssql-jdbc, bundled by upstream Keycloak.
# Installed 13.2.1.jre11 IS the fixed version; trivy mis-parses the ".jre11"
# qualifier and reports it as 13.2.1 < 13.2.1.jre11. Driver is never loaded
# (image is built with --db=postgres). Re-check on next KC bump (added 2026-08-23).
CVE-2025-59250

# CVE-2026-11822, CVE-2026-11824 — sqlite-libs 3.34.1-10.el9_8, bundled by the
# RHEL 9.8 UBI base of upstream quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.7.2. Fixed in
# 3.34.1-11.el9_8. Keycloak does not use SQLite; the lib ships with the UBI
# base image. Both CVEs require attacker-controlled FTS5 queries parsed by
# SQLite, which no Keycloak code path does. Runtime image is ubi9-micro with
# no package manager, so we cannot patch in place. Re-check on next Keycloak
# bump / when upstream rebuilds the 26.7.x base (added 2026-08-27).
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824
